art_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":45,"original_line":45,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1781986637,"original_position":34,"position":34,"subject_type":"line"},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/pulls/21640","id":2099013521,"node_id":"PR_kwDOABZIoc59HGeR","html_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/pull/21640","diff_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/pull/21640.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/pull/21640.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21640","number":21640,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"STY: xsf: apply clang-format","user":{"login":"lucascolley","id":51488791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNDg4Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51488791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley","html_url":"https://github.com/lucascolley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lucascolley/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"body":"#### Reference issue
A more sensible first step towards gh-21024.

#### What does this implement/fix?
Apply clang-format to `scipy/special/xsf`, excluding `/third_party`.

#### Additional information
It was a bit ambitious to try to start applying clang-format across the repo immediately. As noted in https://github.com/scipy/scipy/pull/21024#issuecomment-2185102625, we should probably only do this for non-legacy (and non-vendored) code.

There are a few potential complications (https://github.com/scipy/scipy/pull/21024#issuecomment-2185020182), so easier to take this slow and steady. Here is a start for just `xsf`.

Hopefully this PR will be a good point to make sure we are happy with the config before applying it elsewhere.

cc @izaid @steppi 
