{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417/events","html_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/issues/21417","id":2474654042,"node_id":"I_kwDOABZIoc6TgDla","number":21417,"title":"BUG: special: Unchecked calls of malloc() and calloc() in specfun.h","user":{"login":"WarrenWeckesser","id":321463,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTQ2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/321463?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser","html_url":"https://github.com/WarrenWeckesser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WarrenWeckesser/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":37334597,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzMzNDU5Nw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/labels/defect","name":"defect","color":"e11d21","default":false,"description":"A clear bug or issue that prevents SciPy from being installed or used as expected"},{"id":37340790,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzM0MDc5MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/labels/scipy.special","name":"scipy.special","color":"0366d6","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2024-08-20T03:45:42Z","updated_at":"2024-08-24T08:22:10Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### Describe your issue.

Scattered throughout https://github.com/scipy/scipy/blob/main/scipy/special/xsf/specfun/specfun.h are calls of `malloc()` and `calloc()` where the return values are used without being checked for failure.  That will cause a seg. fault if an allocation does ever fail, which is not correct behavior.  Failures of memory allocation must ultimately raise a `MemoryError`.

We did a lot of work a few years ago to clean up such issues (https://github.com/scipy/scipy/issues/9999).  Perhaps it is time for another audit.

","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/comments/2308186808","html_url":"https://github.com/scipy/scipy/issues/21417#issuecomment-2308186808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scipy/scipy/issues/21417","id":2308186808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOABZIoc6JlCK4","user":{"login":"izaid","id":482179,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjE3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/482179?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid","html_url":"https://github.com/izaid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/izaid/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-08-24T08:22:10Z","updated_at":"2024-08-24T08:22:10Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> > It looks like this occurs in C++ functions with `void` return type. They could be changed to return an `int` status code (eg. 0 means OK, -1 means memory allocation failed). (Or, as @steppi mentioned above, a pointer to a status code could be added as a parameter.) The wrappers must check this and propagate the error code up the wrapping layers until the top level wrapper can detect it and set a Python `MemoryError` exception.
> 
> I see. I didn't realize they all have `void` return type. Yes, we can just change them to return an `int` status code. Right now memory errors are getting lumped into `SF_ERROR_OTHER` in `special`'s error handling,
> 
> e.g.
> 
> ```c++
>     if (eg == NULL) {
>         set_error("prolate_segv", SF_ERROR_OTHER, "memory allocation error");
>         return std::numeric_limits<T>::quiet_NaN();
>     }
> ```
> 
> but we could add `SF_ERROR_MEMORY` to `sf_error.cc` and `sf_error_state.c`. For a first pass, I think it's better to keep these as `SF_ERROR_OTHER` though, and then add a new error state in a follow up.

Chiming in here. We shouldn't change the `void` return type to return an array code, as that actually messes up the direct mapping to ufuncs that we recently put a lot of time into. I actually removed a lot of the old behaviour in which functions returned an error code. I think @steppi's idiom was right:

```
T* u = new (std::nothrow) T[nn + 4];
if (!u) {
    set_error(func_name, SF_ERROR_OTHER, "memory allocation error");
    return std::numeric_limits<T>::quiet_NaN();
}
```

@WarrenWeckesser I see you've been doing various things with special recently, would you also be able to cc me (in addition to @steppi) when you make these issues / PRs? Otherwise I don't necessarily see them. I did a lot of work in `special` recently and there were reasons for some of these changes.

